==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fro|en}} {{term|sutilté|lang=fro}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|subtilitas|subtīlitās|lang=la}}, from {{term|subtilis|subtīlis|subtle|lang=la}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈsʌtəlti/}}
* {{audio|en-us-subtlety.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|subtlet|ies|-}}

# {{context|uncountable}} The quality or fact of being [[subtle]].
#: ''With all his usual '''subtlety''', he quietly fixed the problem before anyone else noticed it.''
# {{context|countable}} An instance of being [[subtle]], a [[subtle]] thing, especially a subtle [[argument]] or [[distinction]].
#: ''The '''subtleties''' of this overture are often overlooked.''
# {{context|countable}} An ornate medieval illusion dish or table decoration, especially when made from one thing but crafted to look like another.
#: ''At the king's coronation feast, several '''subtleties''' were served between main courses.''

